# Environment for `apps/web` — copy to `apps/web/.env` (git-ignored). Next.js loads it for
# `dev`, `build` and `start`; `src/lib/env.ts` validates it and names any variable that is
# missing or malformed.
#
# Every web variable in `.ai-context/architecture.md` → Environment is listed here, and
# `src/lib/env-example.spec.ts` fails if the two drift apart. Uncommented lines are the ones the
# web app reads today. Commented lines are read by a later spec, named above each; uncomment them
# when that spec lands. Secrets are left blank on purpose: never commit a real value here.
#
# Running through Turborepo? Each variable must also be declared in `turbo.json` (strict env
# mode) — `architecture.md` → Environment.

# --- API access ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of `apps/api` as the Next.js server reaches it; the `/api/v1` rewrite proxies here
# (`monorepo-foundation.AC12`). Matches `PORT` in `apps/api/.env.example`.
API_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000

# --- Public site (public-site-rendering) ---------------------------------------------------
# The platform's public origin: portfolios are served at `<this>/<slug>`, and canonical URLs and
# the sitemap are built from it. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` may reach the browser bundle: never a secret.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Shared with the API's publish step (its `REVALIDATE_SECRET`); checked by `/api/revalidate`.
# 32 to 200 characters. Blank: every revalidation call is refused, and pages refresh on their
# 300-second fallback instead.
REVALIDATE_SECRET=

# --- Tooling ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build directory, `.next` when unset. The E2E web server sets `.next-e2e` so it can run beside
# `pnpm dev`; there is no need to set it here.
# NEXT_DIST_DIR=
